  era: "16th c. CE \xB7 Section 34 \xB7 Art and Culture \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Indian music
  text: 'Indian classical music has two great traditions: Hindustani in the north and Carnatic in the south, both built on raga, melody, and tala, rhythm. Tansen, Tyagaraja, Ravi Shankar and M. S. Subbulakshmi are among its celebrated musicians.'
